# WLISTTZ.KEY - every row of a list window chosen (TEST/WLISTT.C
# /MULTI), over the seed's three items and 257 more, 260 rows in a
# window of two; TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/WLISTTZ.SNP, checked by TEST/selchk.py.
# The title ends in the rows chosen, with a * while they are all.
S START
# CTRL-/ chooses all 260; the scroll bar's page, its thumb and its end
# keep them, each window's rows selected.  The last row chosen is item
# 260, and its text is empty, as the list holds its window's rows only.
K CTRL-SLASH
S ALL
K N
S ALLPAGE
K 5
S ALLTHUMB
K SHIFT-F1
S ALLLAST
# An item another station adds (CTRL-A, no move) is not among the rows
# chosen: at the list's end, item 260 is selected and item 261 is not.
K CTRL-A B
S ADDED
# CTRL-\ leaves the focus row alone.  SHIFT-DOWN chooses both rows of
# the window; SHIFT-F1 then gives the last one's own text.
K CTRL-BSLASH
S NONE
K T SHIFT-DOWN
S TWO
K SHIFT-F1
S TWOLAST
# A choice of all whose second request fails (SHIFT-F) says so and
# leaves the two rows chosen, the list counted and the bar as they were;
# so does one that an Esc stops (E).
K SHIFT-F CTRL-SLASH
S FAILBOX
K ENTER
S FAILED
K E CTRL-SLASH
S STOPPED
# With all chosen, a choice stopped keeps them all.
K CTRL-SLASH
S ALLAGAIN
K E CTRL-SLASH
S ALLKEPT
# An empty list (F6's filter) chooses none.
K F6 CTRL-SLASH
S EMPTY
K F6 CTRL-SLASH
S ALLBACK
# A letter's seek ends the choice: 2 finds item 2.
K SHIFT-F4
T 2
S LETTER
# CTRL-O: a window of one row, whose survey stops at its last page
# start, 239 rows counted, the list not counted whole.  A choice of all
# that an Esc stops leaves the bar that range; one that walks as far is
# refused (WL_EOVER, 4), the row chosen kept and the bar too.
K CTRL-O
S ONEROW
K E CTRL-SLASH
S CAPSTOP
K CTRL-SLASH
S CAPOVER
K ESC
